# WBM custom CRS — migrated to PROJ 9 via the legacy init-file mechanism.
#
# PROJ 9 dropped the bundled `epsg` init file, but it STILL honors
# `+init=epsg:CODE` when an `epsg` init file is present in PROJ_DATA. Placing
# this file at $PROJ_DATA/epsg restores the exact behavior the stock v2 (PROJ 6)
# container got from `cat proj.txt >> /usr/share/proj/epsg`.
#
# Verified under GDAL 3.10.3 / PROJ 9.x: `+init=epsg:<CODE>` resolves and real
# gdalwarp reprojection succeeds for all codes below. Full PROJ.4 strings (the
# form WBM bakes into GDAL_test for 8001) also work natively in PROJ 9 with no
# init file — this file is only needed for descriptors that reference the codes
# as `+init=epsg:<CODE>`.
#
# NOTE — 7704 was corrected during migration. The original proj.txt defined it as
#   +proj=stere +lat_0=90 +lat_ts=60 +lon_0=210 +k=90 ...
# specifying BOTH +lat_ts=60 AND +k=90, which is contradictory (a Polar
# Stereographic takes either a standard parallel OR a scale factor, and k=90 is
# not a meaningful scale). PROJ 6 silently tolerated it; PROJ 9 rejects it
# ("lat_ts != lat_0 and k != 1 not supported for Polar Stereographic"). The NDFD
# Alaska grid uses the standard parallel at 60N, so +k=90 is dropped below.

<900918> +proj=sinu +lon_0=0 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +a=6370997.0 +b=6370997.0 +units=m +no_defs <>
#Pnet
<7703> +proj=lcc +lat_1=25 +lat_2=25 +lat_0=0 +lon_0=265 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +a=6371229 +b=6371229 +units=m +no_defs <>
#Alaska Polar Stereographic NDFD (corrected: removed contradictory +k=90)
<7704> +proj=stere +lat_0=90 +lat_ts=60 +lon_0=210 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +a=6371229 +b=6371229 +units=m +no_defs <>
#WRFGEO
<8000> +proj=longlat +ellps=sphere +a=6370000 +b=6370000 +no_defs <>
#WRFLAM-1SP with offset
<8001> +proj=lcc +ellps=sphere +a=6370000.0 +b=6370000.0 +lat_1=41 +lat_0=41 +lon_0=-75 +k_0=1 +x_0=891000.92 +y_0=486000.15 +units=m +no_defs <>
#WRFLAM-2SP with offset
<8002> +proj=lcc +ellps=sphere +a=6370000.0 +b=6370000.0 +lat_1=41 +lat_2=41 +lat_0=41 +lon_0=-75 +x_0=891000.92 +y_0=486000.15 +units=m +no_defs <>
